WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.167 --> 00:00:01.168
The Chestnut Man

00:00:01.251 --> 00:00:04.296
is a gripping new six-part
serial killer thriller

00:00:04.379 --> 00:00:05.506
from Søren Sveistrup,

00:00:05.589 --> 00:00:09.009
the creator Scandi noir
mega hit The Killing.

00:00:09.092 --> 00:00:11.887
It's a pitch-black tale
of murder and mutilation,

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.556
where two detectives
must try to understand

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.059
what links a series
of brutal killings

00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:19.269
to the disappearance
of a politician's daughter

00:00:19.353 --> 00:00:21.980
and why someone is leaving
creepy little figures

00:00:22.064 --> 00:00:24.650
made of sticks and chestnuts
at the crime scenes.

00:00:24.775 --> 00:00:27.319
In this video we will take
a look back at the series

00:00:27.444 --> 00:00:29.154
before examining precisely

00:00:29.238 --> 00:00:33.075
what the end of that twisty,
turny final episode means.

00:00:33.158 --> 00:00:34.493
But just a quick
spoiler warning:

00:00:34.576 --> 00:00:37.037
this video contains details
of the whole story,

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.372
including the ending,

00:00:38.539 --> 00:00:40.082
so if you don't want to know
what happens,

00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:41.166
look away now.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:47.548
The Chestnut Man is based
on Søren Sveistrup’s

00:00:47.631 --> 00:00:50.008
2019 novel of the same name.

00:00:50.092 --> 00:00:51.760
When the body
of a young nurse

00:00:51.844 --> 00:00:53.345
named Laura Kjaer is found,

00:00:53.428 --> 00:00:55.264
ambitious detective
Naia Thulin,

00:00:55.347 --> 00:00:57.140
played by Danica Curcic,

00:00:57.224 --> 00:00:59.393
is brought in
to solve the mystery.

00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:01.311
She becomes obsessed
with the case,

00:01:01.395 --> 00:01:03.063
but her drive to succeed

00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:06.108
risks pushing her away
from her young daughter, Le.

00:01:06.191 --> 00:01:08.318
Helping and sometimes
hindering Thulin

00:01:08.402 --> 00:01:11.613
is Mikkel Boe Følsgaard,
as Detective Mark Hess.

00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:13.282
Although they make
a good team,

00:01:13.365 --> 00:01:15.284
Hess is struggling
with emotional problems

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:17.619
following the death
of his wife and daughter.

00:01:17.703 --> 00:01:18.912
Can he keep it together

00:01:18.996 --> 00:01:20.747
long enough
to solve the mystery

00:01:20.831 --> 00:01:22.708
or will his sometimes rash
behaviour

00:01:22.791 --> 00:01:24.168
get them
kicked off the case?

00:01:25.377 --> 00:01:27.504
As the duo investigate
Kjaer's murder,

00:01:27.588 --> 00:01:30.382
they discover a disturbing
link to a previous case,

00:01:30.465 --> 00:01:33.135
the abduction and apparent
murder of a 12-year-old girl

00:01:33.218 --> 00:01:35.053
named Kristine Hartung.

00:01:35.846 --> 00:01:37.598
Kristine disappeared
a year ago.

00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:39.558
The police
eventually arrested a man,

00:01:39.641 --> 00:01:41.685
Linus Bekker,
who confessed to her murder.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.688
I drove north with
the machete in the car.

00:01:45.397 --> 00:01:46.982
And then I cut her up.

00:01:47.482 --> 00:01:49.651
But he's never revealed
what happened to the body.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:51.945
When Kristine's
fingerprints are found

00:01:52.029 --> 00:01:54.114
on a chestnut man
at a crime scene,

00:01:54.198 --> 00:01:56.408
it raises
the tantalizing question:

00:01:56.491 --> 00:01:58.160
could Kristine
still be alive?

00:01:58.243 --> 00:02:00.662
The timing of all this
seems very deliberate.

00:02:00.746 --> 00:02:01.663
Kristine's mother

00:02:01.747 --> 00:02:03.582
is Denmark's minister
for social affairs,

00:02:03.665 --> 00:02:04.499
Rosa Hartung,

00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:06.460
who has only just
returned to work

00:02:06.543 --> 00:02:08.378
following her daughter's
apparent death.

00:02:08.462 --> 00:02:09.463
Remember Rosa.

00:02:09.546 --> 00:02:11.924
She has a major part
to play in the story.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.052
As Thurin and Hess
investigate,

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.637
they become convinced
that there is

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.056
a definite tie
between the Hartung case

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.016
and the murder
of Laura Kjaer.

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:23.060
But the answer remains
just out of reach,

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:25.354
and the killer
is claiming more victims.

00:02:26.605 --> 00:02:27.773
Like all good mysteries,

00:02:27.856 --> 00:02:29.608
The Chestnut Man
keeps you guessing

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:32.444
as to who did it and why
until the very end.

00:02:32.528 --> 00:02:33.737
As the story unfolds,

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:36.490
we're presented with
numerous possible suspects.

00:02:36.573 --> 00:02:39.117
Early on the detectives
think they've caught a break

00:02:39.201 --> 00:02:41.828
when they bring in a suspect
called Erik Sejer-Lassen.

00:02:41.912 --> 00:02:44.414
We see him stalking a woman
before the police catch him

00:02:44.498 --> 00:02:46.792
and find him with a package
that, when opened,

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:48.377
reveals the hand
of Laura Kjaer.

00:02:49.419 --> 00:02:50.629
But while that might seem

00:02:50.712 --> 00:02:51.922
like a clear sign
of his guilt,

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.341
he seems genuinely
shocked and confused.

00:02:54.424 --> 00:02:57.261
Not only that, but his wife,
Anne, is the next victim,

00:02:57.344 --> 00:03:00.556
killed while Erik is still
in police custody.

00:03:01.265 --> 00:03:02.933
The police let Erik go.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.977
Like Laura,
Anne was survived

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:07.020
by her children,
two young daughters.

00:03:07.104 --> 00:03:09.231
She was having
marital issues,

00:03:09.314 --> 00:03:11.608
likely down to Erik being
a gigantic creep,

00:03:11.692 --> 00:03:13.110
and the police start
to wonder

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:14.570
if there's a link there.

00:03:14.653 --> 00:03:16.029
Perhaps the killer
is murdering

00:03:16.113 --> 00:03:18.824
women he considers
to be neglectful mothers.

00:03:18.907 --> 00:03:21.410
Hess returns to examine
Laura Kjaer's house

00:03:21.493 --> 00:03:22.744
and finds a hidden cellar

00:03:22.828 --> 00:03:25.038
and within it, evidence
that her son, Magnus,

00:03:25.122 --> 00:03:26.999
was being abused
by her boyfriend,

00:03:27.082 --> 00:03:28.667
Hans Henrik Hauge.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:29.418
After a fight,

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.295
where he tries to lock
Hess in the cellar,

00:03:31.378 --> 00:03:34.131
Hauge escapes before
Thulin can arrest him.

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:36.758
But while he's clearly
a dangerous predator,

00:03:36.842 --> 00:03:39.011
there's no evidence
that he's the killer.

00:03:39.094 --> 00:03:40.888
We know from
his early interrogations

00:03:40.971 --> 00:03:42.806
that he has
a rock-solid alibi

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:45.225
for the time of
 Anne Sejer-Lassen's murder.

00:03:45.309 --> 00:03:48.854
Meanwhile, a third potential
victim has been identified.

00:03:48.937 --> 00:03:51.231
The police manage
to get Jessie Kvium

00:03:51.315 --> 00:03:53.358
in time to put her
under protection,

00:03:53.442 --> 00:03:54.359
but it's not enough.

00:03:54.443 --> 00:03:56.737
The killer strikes again
and murders both her

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:59.072
and the officer
assigned to guard her.

00:03:59.156 --> 00:04:01.241
Whoever the mysterious
Chestnut Man is,

00:04:01.325 --> 00:04:04.036
he's always one step ahead
of our detectives,

00:04:04.119 --> 00:04:06.455
almost as if he has
inside information.

00:04:06.538 --> 00:04:08.123
Meanwhile,
Rosa and her husband

00:04:08.207 --> 00:04:09.583
are having
a terrible time of it,

00:04:09.666 --> 00:04:11.710
especially when someone
paints "Murderer"

00:04:11.793 --> 00:04:13.086
on the side of Rosa's car.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:14.087
What could it mean?

00:04:14.171 --> 00:04:16.715
Is someone implying that
she killed her own daughter?

00:04:17.758 --> 00:04:19.301
It turns out
that this is actually

00:04:19.384 --> 00:04:20.469
a bit of a red herring.

00:04:20.552 --> 00:04:22.846
The police eventually
get a tip-off about a woman

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:24.181
named Benedikte Skans

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.641
and when they investigate
her home,

00:04:25.724 --> 00:04:28.560
find evidence that she was
obsessed with Rosa Hartung.

00:04:28.644 --> 00:04:30.145
She has a motive
for harassing her too.

00:04:30.229 --> 00:04:31.897
It's revealed
that some time ago,

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:34.525
Benedikte suffered
a breakdown, which resulted

00:04:34.608 --> 00:04:36.443
in her daughter
being taken from her.

00:04:36.527 --> 00:04:38.070
While she was in recovery,
however,

00:04:38.153 --> 00:04:40.239
her daughter died
from a lung infection.

00:04:40.322 --> 00:04:43.575
Consumed by grief, Benedikte
and partner Jacob Rasouli

00:04:43.659 --> 00:04:46.078
who, in a shock twist, turns
out to be Rosa's driver,

00:04:46.161 --> 00:04:48.121
plans to get revenge
on the Hartungs.

00:04:48.205 --> 00:04:50.207
by abducting their son,
Gustav.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.501
The kidnappers succeed
and take young Gustav

00:04:52.584 --> 00:04:53.961
deep into the forest.

00:04:54.044 --> 00:04:55.587
Benedikte plans
to murder him,

00:04:55.671 --> 00:04:56.797
but Jacob is less sure.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.550
He wants to get back at
Rosa, but not kill a child.

00:04:59.633 --> 00:05:02.678
As they argue, a mysterious
car pulls up nearby.

00:05:03.428 --> 00:05:05.264
Meanwhile, the police
have somehow managed

00:05:05.347 --> 00:05:07.015
to locate the kidnappers.

00:05:07.099 --> 00:05:09.726
- almost as if one of them
has some inside knowledge

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:10.394
on this whole thing -

00:05:10.477 --> 00:05:13.647
and get to the woods in time
to find young Gustav

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:14.565
alive and well,

00:05:14.648 --> 00:05:17.359
but both Benedikte Skans
and Jacob Rasouli dead.

00:05:17.442 --> 00:05:18.277
The police,

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:20.487
keen to wrap the case up
as quickly as possible,

00:05:20.571 --> 00:05:22.614
conclude that this was
a murder suicide,

00:05:22.698 --> 00:05:25.534
that Benedikte killed Jacob
and then took her own life.

00:05:25.617 --> 00:05:27.786
The official word is
that Skans and Rasouli

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:29.288
were the chestnut men
killers.

00:05:29.371 --> 00:05:30.956
Kristine really is dead.

00:05:31.039 --> 00:05:32.791
The case is closed.

00:05:32.875 --> 00:05:35.169
But the detectives
remain unconvinced.

00:05:35.252 --> 00:05:36.253
Time passes,

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:38.839
but both Hess and Thurin
remain troubled by the case

00:05:38.922 --> 00:05:41.049
and a sense
of unfinished business.

00:05:41.133 --> 00:05:43.260
Rosa, too, is worried
and beset by dreams

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:45.053
of two children
from her past,

00:05:45.137 --> 00:05:46.805
Toke and Astrid Bering.

00:05:46.889 --> 00:05:49.725
Toke and Astrid were
foster kids who came to stay

00:05:49.808 --> 00:05:52.311
with Rosa and her
adoptive parents in 1985.

00:05:52.394 --> 00:05:54.521
But Rosa didn't like
sharing their affection

00:05:54.605 --> 00:05:56.231
and so lied to her parents,
telling them

00:05:56.315 --> 00:05:58.317
that Toke and Astrid
had done something bad,

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.694
though we don't find out
exactly what she said.

00:06:00.777 --> 00:06:03.614
The siblings were quickly
moved on to another family.

00:06:03.697 --> 00:06:05.782
Meanwhile, Hess
is researching a massacre

00:06:05.866 --> 00:06:08.452
that took place in 1987
at a farmhouse

00:06:08.535 --> 00:06:10.370
that belonged
to a man named Ørum.

00:06:10.454 --> 00:06:11.872
The police found
five bodies:

00:06:11.955 --> 00:06:13.498
two adults, two teenagers,

00:06:13.582 --> 00:06:15.667
and the first cop
to arrive on the scene,

00:06:15.751 --> 00:06:16.585
Marius Larsen.

00:06:16.668 --> 00:06:18.045
All killed with a shotgun.

00:06:18.128 --> 00:06:19.713
In the basement
of the building,

00:06:19.796 --> 00:06:21.423
they found
two cowering children

00:06:21.507 --> 00:06:23.300
and a whole lot
of chestnut men.

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:24.676
It turns out
that the Ørum family

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:27.137
had taken in
Toke and Astrid Bering

00:06:27.221 --> 00:06:29.223
after they left
the Hartung's care.

00:06:29.306 --> 00:06:31.183
While it seemed like
an altruistic act

00:06:31.266 --> 00:06:32.267
from the outside,

00:06:32.351 --> 00:06:34.853
they were keeping them
imprisoned, abusing them

00:06:34.937 --> 00:06:37.523
and forcing the boy, Toke,
to make chestnut men.

00:06:37.606 --> 00:06:39.191
At the time,
the police assumed

00:06:39.274 --> 00:06:41.276
that Ørum had been
responsible for the massacre

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:42.778
before shooting himself.

00:06:42.861 --> 00:06:44.530
But Hess had
a different idea.

00:06:44.613 --> 00:06:46.657
What if the young Toke
was responsible

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.325
for the farmhouse killings?

00:06:48.408 --> 00:06:50.911
He digs deeper and makes
a startling discovery.

00:06:50.994 --> 00:06:53.247
The adult Toke Bering
looks an awful lot

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:54.873
like Thurin's friend
and colleague,

00:06:54.957 --> 00:06:56.500
forensic scientist
Simon Genz,

00:06:56.583 --> 00:06:58.794
who has been
helping them on the case.

00:06:58.877 --> 00:07:00.963
That explains
how the killer was always

00:07:01.046 --> 00:07:03.048
able to stay one step
ahead of the police.

00:07:03.131 --> 00:07:04.800
He was
one of them the whole time.

00:07:04.883 --> 00:07:06.510
Thurin realizes this too,

00:07:06.593 --> 00:07:08.428
but unfortunately
it's too late to stop him

00:07:08.512 --> 00:07:10.806
from Chloroforming her
and tying her up

00:07:10.889 --> 00:07:12.391
in Toke Bering's
childhood home.

00:07:13.183 --> 00:07:15.978
Toke Bering, Simon Genz,
the Chestnut Man,

00:07:16.061 --> 00:07:17.145
whatever you want
to call him,

00:07:17.229 --> 00:07:19.773
has been plotting revenge
on Rosa all the time.

00:07:19.857 --> 00:07:21.358
He blames her for the abuse

00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:23.527
that he and Astrid
suffered as kids.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:24.945
He kidnapped Kristine,

00:07:25.028 --> 00:07:26.738
and the murders
of the other women

00:07:26.822 --> 00:07:28.323
who he saw as unfit mothers

00:07:28.407 --> 00:07:31.785
all fits into his long plan
to taunt Rosa further

00:07:31.869 --> 00:07:32.703
before killing her.

00:07:32.786 --> 00:07:34.371
Luckily he hasn't counted

00:07:34.454 --> 00:07:36.206
on the detectives'
resourcefulness.

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:37.958
Hess turns up
in the nick of time

00:07:38.041 --> 00:07:39.168
and goes after Toke,

00:07:39.251 --> 00:07:40.627
who is holding Thurin
captive.

00:07:40.711 --> 00:07:41.795
There's a chase,

00:07:41.879 --> 00:07:44.006
but it goes badly wrong
for the Chestnut Man,

00:07:44.089 --> 00:07:46.758
who ends up rather aptly
impaled on a tree.

00:07:46.842 --> 00:07:48.719
He dies, refusing to say

00:07:48.802 --> 00:07:50.596
whether Kristine
is still alive or not.

00:07:50.679 --> 00:07:52.055
But just as all seems lost,

00:07:52.139 --> 00:07:53.432
there's a call
on Toke's phone.

00:07:53.515 --> 00:07:55.434
The detectives trace it
back to Poland

00:07:55.517 --> 00:07:57.227
and Toke's sister, Astrid.

00:07:57.311 --> 00:07:59.396
The police arrest Astrid
and find,

00:07:59.521 --> 00:08:01.565
scared but alive,
Kristine Hartung,

00:08:01.648 --> 00:08:04.109
who is finally reunited
with her family.

00:08:05.068 --> 00:08:06.570
It's a heart-warming
conclusion

00:08:06.653 --> 00:08:07.946
to this pitch-black tale.

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:10.282
And yet, there remains
troubling undercurrents.

00:08:10.365 --> 00:08:13.118
Hess has proven himself
as a detective

00:08:13.202 --> 00:08:15.329
and helped reunite
a family with a child

00:08:15.412 --> 00:08:17.080
they never thought
they would see again.

00:08:17.164 --> 00:08:18.582
But he will continue
to grieve

00:08:18.665 --> 00:08:20.167
his lost wife and daughter.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:22.294
And more troubling,
as the story ends,

00:08:22.377 --> 00:08:23.754
we learn that Linus Bekker

00:08:23.837 --> 00:08:25.464
has been freed from prison.

00:08:25.547 --> 00:08:27.299
He may not have killed
Kristine,

00:08:27.382 --> 00:08:29.760
but he is a self-proclaimed
chosen one.

00:08:29.843 --> 00:08:32.221
We're left wondering,
might he one day take on

00:08:32.304 --> 00:08:34.681
the mantle
of the Chestnut Man himself?

